+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Full-layer VERIFY (q_len 8, causal inside the block) at 1 < batch <= 64 (tp8, page 1): rewrite
+# stage 6, in its OWN load_inline modules (muse_full_verify_wgmma_s6 for the two routed candidates,
+# muse_full_verify_wgmma_s6d for the prepare-only DIAG designs) so a build or self-check failure here
+# never touches another module. Any failure, refusal or deadline leaves full verify on master's PAIRED
+# FA3 path (the `paired` predicate in kernel_fn stays true when the route table has no entry).
+#
+# SOURCE: s5 (full-verify-wgmma-s5-qfrag-reload, 71e40388): FP8 QK wgmma m64n64k32 with Q staged in smem and
+# reloaded before every tile's S, Max_offset-8 FP8 P, the per-warpgroup V^T transpose, stream-K over 64-token
+# tiles, the in-kernel ticket combine + paired norm-gate, the error word and the bounded mbarrier waits, all
+# verbatim. s5 was correct but 288.7 vs paired FA3 164.4 us at B=16 (429.5 vs 302.4 at B=32): 2x the bytes cost
+# 1.49x the time. Only the PIPELINE OWNERSHIP changes here:
+#  * RING (the adversarial review's design, which wins over the spec's SWIZZLE_64B half-row rings): the ring
+#    is s5's EXACT 4-stage SW128 128-B-row ring with the same descriptors, but each stage's two 64-B head
+#    halves have their own FULL / EMPTY mbarrier pair (128 arrivals, one warpgroup). Warpgroup g's 128
+#    threads fill ONLY head g's half (4 x 16-B cp.async.cg per tile per thread; one warp-wide instruction now
+#    covers 16 full 32-B sectors instead of s5's 8 half-sectors) and wait only for their own half, and each
+#    warpgroup prefetches its own page indices (16-tile blocks, private block pair), so there is no
+#    cross-warpgroup wait anywhere in the tile loop.
+#  * SMEM: s5's non-ring smem is ~34.4 KB (the spec's 6-stage 96 KB ring cannot hold 2 CTAs/SM), so the
+#    2-CTA/SM variant keeps 4 stages; the per-warpgroup page-index blocks add 8 KB (108,192 B per CTA, 2 fit).
+#  * OVL: variant 0 (OVL=0) = the split ring + s5's serial S -> transpose -> softmax -> PV chain at
+#    __launch_bounds__(256, 2), grid 2 x SM. Variant 1 (OVL=1) = the split ring + S(n + 1) issued (FULL(n + 1)
+#    waited) before softmax(n), a second 64x64 fp32 S accumulator, __launch_bounds__(256, 1), grid SM,
+#    12 stages if the layout fits the 232448 B block limit, else 10 (it does not fit at 12 with the
+#    per-warpgroup page-index blocks, so 10; the build prints the numbers).
+#  * DIAG (prepare-only, never routed, never timed in kernel_fn): gather-only instantiations of s5's CTA-wide ring,
+#    the split ring at 2 CTAs/SM and the split ring at 1 CTA/SM, each with and without the ticket epilogue, plus
+#    s5's full kernel, timed at B = 8 / 16 / 32 with the fit T = a + b * tiles/CTA printed.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
